{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Library-target","text":"Library target"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"text":" ships as its own product in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":" package. Add it to a target’s dependencies in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"text":" and import it where you wire the plugin:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import SwiduxKillswitch"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The target depends on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":" and links against ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIKit"},{"text":" on iOS \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppKit"},{"text":" on macOS for the default URL-opening behavior.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Types","text":"Types"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"KillswitchPlugin","text":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The domain plugin. Conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPlugin"},{"text":" and is generic over the host app’s root state and action types.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["@MainActor","public struct KillswitchPlugin<RootState, RootAction>: SwiduxPlugin {","    public typealias State = RootState","    public typealias Action = RootAction","","    public init(","        state: WritableKeyPath<RootState, KillswitchState>,","        action toRootAction: @escaping @Sendable (KillswitchAction) -> RootAction,","        extractAction: @escaping @Sendable (RootAction) -> KillswitchAction?,","        service: KillswitchService,","        appVersion: @escaping @Sendable () -> String,","        openURL: @escaping @Sendable (URL) async -> Void = { \/* UIApplication \/ NSWorkspace *\/ }","    )","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The default ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"openURL"},{"text":" calls ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIApplication.shared.open(_:)"},{"text":" on iOS and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSWorkspace.shared.open(_:)"},{"text":" on macOS, both hopped to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MainActor"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"KillswitchState","text":"KillswitchState"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The state slice the plugin owns. Default-constructed values match a fresh, never-fetched session.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["public struct KillswitchState: Sendable, Equatable {","    public var verdict: KillswitchVerdict   \/\/ defaults to .unknown","    public var lastFetch: Date?             \/\/ nil until first successful fetch","    public var fetchError: String?          \/\/ localized description of last failure","","    public var isBlocked: Bool              \/\/ delegates to verdict.isBlocked","    public var canOpenUpdateURL: Bool       \/\/ .blocked AND updateURL is non-nil","","    public init(","        verdict: KillswitchVerdict = .unknown,","        lastFetch: Date? = nil,","        fetchError: String? = nil","    )","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isBlocked"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canOpenUpdateURL"},{"text":" are convenience computed properties. Bind UI off them rather than pattern-matching ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verdict"},{"text":" everywhere.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"KillswitchAction","text":"KillswitchAction"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin’s local action enum. Wrap these in your root action through the case you provide at registration.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["public enum KillswitchAction: Sendable {","    case fetch","    case forceFetch","    case verdictReceived(KillswitchVerdict, fromNetwork: Bool)","    case fetchFailed(String)","    case openUpdateURL","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".fetch"},{"text":" is the launch-time entry point — it consults the cache and skips the network when the cached config is fresh. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".forceFetch"},{"text":" always hits the network, suitable for pull-to-refresh or post-update health checks.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"KillswitchService","text":"KillswitchService"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A closure-based service that fetches and caches the remote config. Substitute the live factory in production and the mock factory in tests.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["public struct KillswitchService: Sendable {","    public var fetch: @Sendable () async throws -> KillswitchConfig","    public var loadCached: @Sendable () -> KillswitchConfig?","    public var saveCached: @Sendable (KillswitchConfig) -> Void","    public let cacheLifetime: TimeInterval","","    public init(","        fetch: @escaping @Sendable () async throws -> KillswitchConfig,","        loadCached: @escaping @Sendable () -> KillswitchConfig?,","        saveCached: @escaping @Sendable (KillswitchConfig) -> Void,","        cacheLifetime: TimeInterval","    )","","    public static func live(","        endpoint: URL,","        fetchTimeout: TimeInterval = 10,","        cacheLifetime: TimeInterval = 3600,","        session: URLSession = .shared","    ) -> KillswitchService","","    public static func mock(","        result: @escaping @Sendable () async throws -> KillswitchConfig = { KillswitchConfig() },","        cached: KillswitchConfig? = nil,","        cacheLifetime: TimeInterval = 3600","    ) -> KillswitchService","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"live(endpoint:)"},{"text":" decodes JSON from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"endpoint"},{"text":" with a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reloadIgnoringLocalCacheData"},{"text":" policy and persists the result to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swidux-killswitch.json"},{"text":" in a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"bundle-scoped subdirectory"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" of the user’s caches directory. The stored payload records the endpoint it came from, and a cache written for a different endpoint reads as absent — the cached config produces a verdict with the same authority a fetched one does, so it is scoped and checked rather than trusted. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" §6a. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mock(result:cached:)"},{"text":" keeps an in-memory cache and lets a test inject a closure that returns or throws.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The endpoint must be ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"HTTPS"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http"},{"text":" is allowed only for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localhost"},{"text":" development servers; anything else is a precondition failure) — the killswitch is a remote control channel and must not be tamperable in transit. Non-2xx responses and payloads over 1 MB are treated as fetch failures, which fall back to the cache (and ultimately fail open).","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"KillswitchConfig","text":"KillswitchConfig"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The decoded shape of the remote JSON. All fields are optional — a config with every field ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" evaluates to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".allowed"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"code":["public struct KillswitchConfig: Codable, Sendable, Equatable {","    public var minimumSupportedVersion: String?","    public var blockedVersions: [String]?","    public var blockedRanges: [String]?","    public var blockedTitle: String?","    public var blockedMessage: String?","    public var updateURL: String?","","    public init(","        minimumSupportedVersion: String? = nil,","        blockedVersions: [String]? = nil,","        blockedRanges: [String]? = nil,","        blockedTitle: String? = nil,","        blockedMessage: String? = nil,","        updateURL: String? = nil","    )","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"KillswitchVerdict","text":"KillswitchVerdict"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The result of evaluating a config against the running version.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["public enum KillswitchVerdict: Sendable, Equatable {","    case unknown","    case allowed","    case blocked(title: String?, message: String?, updateURL: URL?)","","    public var isBlocked: Bool","","    public static func evaluate(","        _ config: KillswitchConfig,","        against currentVersionString: String","    ) -> KillswitchVerdict","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"text":" is the initial state before any fetch has been attempted. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"evaluate(_:against:)"},{"text":" always returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".allowed"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".blocked(...)"},{"text":" — never ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isBlocked"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":" only for the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".blocked"},{"text":" case.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"SemanticVersion","text":"SemanticVersion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A SemVer 2.0.0 parser used internally to compare versions. Public so you can construct or compare versions directly in tests.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["public struct SemanticVersion: Sendable, Hashable, Comparable {","    public let major: Int","    public let minor: Int","    public let patch: Int","    public let prerelease: [PrereleaseIdentifier]","","    public init(","        major: Int,","        minor: Int,","        patch: Int,","        prerelease: [PrereleaseIdentifier] = []","    )","","    public init?(_ string: String)","","    public enum PrereleaseIdentifier: Sendable, Hashable, Comparable {","        case numeric(Int)","        case alphanumeric(String)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The string initializer accepts ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"1.2.3\""},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"1.2.3-beta.1\""},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"1.2.3-beta.1+build42\""},{"text":". Build metadata after ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"+"},{"text":" is parsed and discarded. Malformed input returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Comparison follows the SemVer 2.0.0 precedence rules: numeric major\/minor\/patch first, then prerelease (a version with a prerelease tag has lower precedence than the same version without), then prerelease identifiers compared left-to-right with numeric identifiers ordering before alphanumeric.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"VersionRange","text":"VersionRange"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A half-open range ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[lowerBound, upperBound)"},{"text":" of semantic versions, used to express ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"blockedRanges"},{"text":" entries.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["public struct VersionRange: Sendable, Hashable {","    public let lowerBound: SemanticVersion","    public let upperBound: SemanticVersion","","    public init?(lowerBound: SemanticVersion, upperBound: SemanticVersion)","    public init?(_ string: String)   \/\/ parses \"a.b.c..<x.y.z\"","","    public func contains(_ version: SemanticVersion) -> Bool","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Both initializers fail and return ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" if the lower bound is not strictly less than the upper bound, or if either side cannot be parsed.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Action-semantics","text":"Action semantics"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effect on state"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returned effect"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".fetch"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"none"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"if the cache is fresh ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date() - lastFetch < cacheLifetime"},{"type":"text","text":" AND "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCached()"},{"type":"text","text":" is non-nil), evaluates the cached config and dispatches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".verdictReceived(...)"},{"type":"text","text":" without hitting the network; otherwise behaves like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".forceFetch"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".forceFetch"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"none"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service.fetch()"},{"type":"text","text":", persists the result via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service.saveCached(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", dispatches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".verdictReceived(...)"},{"type":"text","text":". On thrown error, falls back to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service.loadCached()"},{"type":"text","text":" if available — dispatching "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".verdictReceived(...)"},{"type":"text","text":" from the cache "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".fetchFailed(message)"},{"type":"text","text":" so the UI can surface the error while keeping a usable verdict"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".verdictReceived(verdict, fromNetwork:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"sets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verdict"},{"type":"text","text":", clears "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fetchError"},{"type":"text","text":"; sets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lastFetch = Date()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"only when ","type":"text"},{"code":"fromNetwork","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is true","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — a cache-served verdict must not slide the freshness window, or a session polling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".fetch"},{"type":"text","text":" inside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cacheLifetime"},{"type":"text","text":" would never consult the network again"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"none"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".fetchFailed(message)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"sets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fetchError = message"},{"type":"text","text":" (does not clear "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verdict"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lastFetch"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"none"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".openUpdateURL"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"none"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"if "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verdict"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".blocked"},{"type":"text","text":" with a non-nil "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"updateURL"},{"type":"text","text":" whose scheme is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"itms-apps"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"macappstore"},{"type":"text","text":", calls the plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"openURL"},{"type":"text","text":" closure; otherwise no effect (the URL comes from remote config, so arbitrary schemes are never opened)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin only handles its own actions. Any action that ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"extractAction"},{"text":" returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" for is ignored — the plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(...)"},{"text":" returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" immediately.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The combination of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".forceFetch"},{"text":"’s cached-fallback behavior and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".fetch"},{"text":"‘s cache-freshness gate is the basis for the plugin’s offline tolerance: a launch on a flaky network still yields a verdict (cached) and an error indicator (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fetchError"},{"text":"), without leaving the UI stuck on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".verdictReceived"},{"type":"text","text":" is dispatched on every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".fetch"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".forceFetch"},{"type":"text","text":" (cache hit or network), usually with an unchanged verdict. Consume verdict transitions by observing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchState"},{"type":"text","text":" or a value derived from it — not by mapping this action. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture#Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Verdict-evaluation-rules","text":"Verdict evaluation rules"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchVerdict.evaluate(_:against:)"},{"text":" is fail-open: any unparseable input yields ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".allowed"},{"text":". Checks run in this fixed order, returning ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".blocked(...)"},{"text":" on the first match:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Current version parse."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" If ","type":"text"},{"code":"currentVersionString","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cannot be parsed as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SemanticVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", return ","type":"text"},{"code":".allowed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" immediately.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Minimum supported version."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" If ","type":"text"},{"code":"config.minimumSupportedVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parses and ","type":"text"},{"code":"currentVersion < minVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", return ","type":"text"},{"code":".blocked(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explicit blocked versions."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Iterate ","type":"text"},{"code":"config.blockedVersions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If any entry parses and equals ","type":"text"},{"code":"currentVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", return ","type":"text"},{"code":".blocked(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Blocked ranges."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Iterate ","type":"text"},{"code":"config.blockedRanges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If any entry parses as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"VersionRange","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and contains ","type":"text"},{"code":"currentVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", return ","type":"text"},{"code":".blocked(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Otherwise"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" return ","type":"text"},{"code":".allowed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A blocked verdict carries the config’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"blockedTitle"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"blockedMessage"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"updateURL"},{"text":" (parsed via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URL(string:)"},{"text":") regardless of which check matched.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Remote-config-JSON-shape","text":"Remote config JSON shape"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeV